# notko

Fallibility primitives for `no_std` rust, and the type-level list the rest of the stack builds its
products on. Everything here is no alloc and, in the default build of the primitives, has no
dependencies at all.

The repository holds five crates. `notko` is the carriers themselves, `Just`, `Maybe` and `Outcome`,
with the const and plain paths beside each other. `notko-hlist` is the type-level list and the product
over it. `notko-macros` is the `#[profile]` attribute, which rewrites a function onto one of the
carriers, and `notko-macros-core` is the expansion behind it, kept apart so it can be tested without a
proc-macro boundary in the way. `notko-build` is the build-script helper for a tier defined in one
crate and used in another.

There is no canon declared for notko. The designs under `docs/design/` stand in for one, and where
they are silent the question goes to the maintainer rather than being decided in code.
